OL,4,CMajor US storms snarl air travel as    
OL,5,Cmore than 800,000 left in the dark on  
OL,6,CThanksgiving holiday                   
OL,7,GMajor storms bring severe weather to   
OL,8,Gboth US coasts, causing power cuts and 
OL,9,Gflight cancellations as the country    
OL,10,Gcelebrates Thanksgiving.               
OL,12,FHundreds of flights have been          
OL,13,Fcancelled, with more than 1,000        
OL,14,Fdelayed, meanwhile more than 800,000   
OL,15,Fcustomers are without power.           
OL,17,FIt comes as more than 80 million       
OL,18,Fpeople are expected to travel over the 
OL,19,Fholiday weekend - Transportation       
OL,20,FSecretary Sean Duffy calls it "the     
OL,21,FSuper Bowl of US air travel".          
